#ifndef STEEM_HARDFORK_0_27
#define STEEM_HARDFORK_0_27 27

// MELEK content & curation rewards fix (HF27).
//
// THE BUG THIS FIXES: no author or curation reward has EVER been paid on MELEK mainnet. Every
// account on the chain reports posting_rewards == 0 and curation_rewards == 0, from genesis
// (2026-07-12) onward, while the "post" reward fund has swollen past 730,000 MELEK because
// nothing ever leaves it. Posts reach cashout normally — cashout_time flips to the "settled"
// sentinel — and credit nothing.
//
// WHY: cashout_comment_helper() guards the payout with two conversions through the MBD median
// price feed, and util::to_sbd()/util::to_steem() BOTH return zero when that price is null:
//
//     if( util::to_sbd( current_steem_price, asset( reward, STEEM_SYMBOL ) ) < STEEM_MIN_PAYOUT_SBD )
//        reward = 0;                                             // 0.000 MBD < 0.020 MBD  -> always true
//     uint64_t max_steem = util::to_steem( current_steem_price, comment.max_accepted_payout ).amount.value;
//     reward = std::min( reward, max_steem );                    // max_steem == 0          -> always zero
//
// So the payout is zeroed twice over, independently.
//
// AND THE PRICE CAN NEVER BE NON-NULL ON THIS CHAIN. update_median_feed() only writes a median
// when feeds.size() >= STEEM_MIN_FEEDS, and MELEK defines STEEM_MIN_FEEDS as
// STEEM_MAX_WITNESSES/3 == 7 (stock Steem uses /7 == 3). The chain has FIVE witness accounts
// (maat, seshat, thoth, hathor, initminer; num_scheduled_witnesses == 5), so at most five feeds
// can ever be collected. 5 < 7, permanently. No witness has ever published a feed either
// (last_sbd_exchange_update == 1970-01-01 on all five), but publishing would not help.
//
// This is not a misconfiguration — it is vestigial Steem machinery on a chain that deliberately
// has no second token. CLAUDE.md: "Single token: MELEK is the only on-chain token. No SBD/HBD/BBD
// equivalent, no stablecoin pair, no internal currency conversion logic. Witnesses publish price
// feeds informationally." current_sbd_supply is 0.000 MBD and STEEM_SBD_START_PERCENT_HF20 is 0,
// so no MBD exists or will ever be printed. The chain's own stated design — "every MELEK in
// circulation must be earned through block production, content rewards, or curation rewards" —
// has therefore been violated since launch: only block production has ever paid.
//
// WHAT HF27 DOES: when the median price is null, skip both MBD-denominated guards. The only part
// of that logic with meaning on a single-token chain is max_accepted_payout == 0, i.e. an author
// explicitly declining payout, which is preserved exactly.
//
// WHY GATED: this changes payout amounts, so patched and unpatched nodes would compute different
// state and fork apart. Gating keeps every pre-HF27 block replaying exactly as it was produced
// (a from-genesis replay must still reproduce the zero payouts that really happened) and flips
// the rule for all upgraded nodes together at the HF27 block.
//
// NOT RETROACTIVE: comments already settled at zero are settled. Only comments whose cashout
// falls at or after the HF27 block can pay. Set the activation time accordingly — every hour of
// delay permanently zeroes more posts that are currently inside their 7-day window.
#ifdef IS_TEST_NET
#define STEEM_HARDFORK_0_27_TIME 1            // testnet/devnet: active immediately on the upgraded binary
#else
#define STEEM_HARDFORK_0_27_TIME 1924992000   // mainnet: PLACEHOLDER (2031-01-01 00:00 UTC). SET A REAL COORDINATED TIME before deploy — see HARDFORK_BUNDLE.md.
#endif

#define STEEM_HARDFORK_0_27_VERSION hardfork_version( 0, 27 )

#endif
